# Quaked agent instructions

On the owner's host, read the standing instructions in `/Users/bri/agent.md` for collaboration, task coordination, verification, preservation and follow-up. Those instructions continue to apply; this file adds project-specific routing. On another host use its supplied owner instructions; do not infer new authority from a missing local path.

## Texture work

Before auditing, generating, replacing, repairing, deriving maps for or registering Quake/Hexen textures, read [the texture-authoring skill](skills/quaked-texture-authoring/SKILL.md) and its relevant references. It applies to Quake and its official expansions, Hexen II and Portal of Praevus. Use the existing tools and actual current campaign records; do not reconstruct the process from a stale transcript or invent another authoring pipeline.

A texture must visibly depict a recognisable real-world material. High resolution, sharpness, discernible detail, numerical similarity or a “photorealistic” prompt label alone is insufficient. Preserve original colour, style, forms and feature scale while making the chosen physical material convincing. Keep unreadable/abstract/grainy results on HOLD.

The shared output contract is [docs/texture-tier-standard.md](docs/texture-tier-standard.md): unchanged Low, default Mid 4× and High 8× derived directly from one retained master, matching uncompressed-master relief and enhanced maps at lossy WebP Q92, method 6. Follow the skill for exact source/alias proof, generation journaling, material/relief gates, half/quarter comparisons, repeats, repair, cleanup and safe Dev checkpoints. Special native families require their own semantics; ordinary WORLD coverage is not campaign completion.

For unrelated engine or product work, preserve the existing architecture and apply the standing owner instructions. Loading this skill does not grant release, provider, spending or other-project authority.
